# Docker Deployment & Containerization

## 🐳 Docker Architecture

### Container Structure
The application uses a multi-container architecture with Docker Compose:

- **Backend Container**: FastAPI application with Python dependencies
- **Frontend Container**: React application served by Nginx
- **PostgreSQL Container**: Database for job persistence
- **Redis Container**: Caching and job queue (optional but recommended)

### Docker Files Location
- **Backend**: [docker/Dockerfile.backend](mdc:docker/Dockerfile.backend)
- **Frontend**: [docker/Dockerfile.frontend](mdc:docker/Dockerfile.frontend)  
- **Compose**: [docker/docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker/docker-compose.yml)
- **Database Init**: [docker/init-db.sql](mdc:docker/init-db.sql)

## 🚀 Quick Deployment

### Production Deployment
```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/your-repo/ai-video-generator.git
cd ai-video-generator

# Start all services
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up --build -d

# Access services
# Frontend: http://localhost:5173
# Backend API: http://localhost:8080
# Database: localhost:5432
# Redis: localhost:6379
```

### Development Deployment
```bash
# Start with development overrides
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml -f docker/docker-compose.dev.yml up --build

# Or start individual services
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up postgres redis -d
# Then run backend/frontend locally for development
```

## 🔧 Environment Configuration

### Required Environment Variables
Create `.env` file in project root:

```bash
# === REQUIRED ===
# Database (PostgreSQL)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://videohelper_user:videohelper_password@postgres:5432/videohelper

# API Keys (at least one AI key required)
PEXELS_API_KEY=your_pexels_api_key
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_google_api_key
# OR
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key

# === OPTIONAL ===
# Security
API_KEY=your_secret_api_key
CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS=*

# Redis (for enhanced performance)
REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0

# Performance
MAX_CONCURRENT_JOBS=4
VIDEOHELPER_MAX_CONCURRENT_JOBS=4

# Monitoring
ENABLE_METRICS=true
METRICS_PORT=9090
SENTRY_DSN=your_sentry_dsn

# Storage
VIDEOHELPER_OUTPUT_DIR=/app/output
CACHE_DIR=/app/cache
MAX_CACHE_SIZE_GB=10
```

### Docker Compose Environment
The compose file uses environment variable substitution:

```yaml
# docker/docker-compose.yml
services:
  backend:
    environment:
      - DATABASE_URL=${DATABASE_URL:-postgresql://videohelper_user:videohelper_password@postgres:5432/videohelper}
      - PEXELS_API_KEY=${PEXELS_API_KEY}
      - GOOGLE_API_KEY=${GOOGLE_API_KEY}
      - REDIS_URL=${REDIS_URL:-redis://redis:6379/0}
      - API_KEY=${API_KEY}
```

## 📦 Container Configuration

### Backend Container
```dockerfile
# docker/Dockerfile.backend
FROM python:3.10-slim

# System dependencies
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    ffmpeg \
    espeak-ng \
    git \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# Python dependencies
COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

# Application code
WORKDIR /app
COPY backend/ ./backend/
COPY . .

# Health check
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=10s --start-period=5s --retries=3 \
    CMD curl -f http://localhost:8080/api/health || exit 1

# Run application
CMD ["uvicorn", "backend.app:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8080"]
```

### Frontend Container
```dockerfile
# docker/Dockerfile.frontend
FROM node:18-alpine as builder

WORKDIR /app
COPY frontend/package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --only=production

COPY frontend/ .
RUN npm run build

# Production stage
FROM nginx:alpine
COPY --from=builder /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html
COPY docker/nginx.conf /etc/nginx/nginx.conf

EXPOSE 80
CMD ["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]
```

### Database Container
```yaml
# PostgreSQL with initialization
postgres:
  image: postgres:15-alpine
  environment:
    POSTGRES_DB: videohelper
    POSTGRES_USER: videohelper_user  
    POSTGRES_PASSWORD: videohelper_password
  volumes:
    - postgres_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    - ./init-db.sql:/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/init-db.sql
  ports:
    - "5432:5432"
  healthcheck:
    test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U videohelper_user -d videohelper"]
    interval: 10s
    timeout: 5s
    retries: 5
```

## 🔄 Service Orchestration

### Complete Docker Compose
```yaml
version: '3.8'

services:
  # Backend API
  backend:
    build:
      context: ..
      dockerfile: docker/Dockerfile.backend
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"
    environment:
      - DATABASE_URL=postgresql://videohelper_user:videohelper_password@postgres:5432/videohelper
      - REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0
      - PEXELS_API_KEY=${PEXELS_API_KEY}
      - GOOGLE_API_KEY=${GOOGLE_API_KEY}
    volumes:
      - ../output:/app/output
      - ../cache:/app/cache
      - ../logs:/app/logs
      - ../temp:/app/temp
    depends_on:
      postgres:
        condition: service_healthy
      redis:
        condition: service_healthy
    restart: unless-stopped
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "curl", "-f", "http://localhost:8080/api/health"]
      interval: 30s
      timeout: 10s
      retries: 3

  # Frontend UI  
  frontend:
    build:
      context: ..
      dockerfile: docker/Dockerfile.frontend
    ports:
      - "5173:80"
    environment:
      - VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8080
    depends_on:
      - backend
    restart: unless-stopped

  # PostgreSQL Database
  postgres:
    image: postgres:15-alpine
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: videohelper
      POSTGRES_USER: videohelper_user
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: videohelper_password
    volumes:
      - postgres_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
      - ../init-db.sql:/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/init-db.sql
    ports:
      - "5432:5432"
    restart: unless-stopped
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U videohelper_user -d videohelper"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5

  # Redis Cache
  redis:
    image: redis:7-alpine
    ports:
      - "6379:6379"
    volumes:
      - redis_data:/data
    restart: unless-stopped
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "redis-cli", "ping"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 3

volumes:
  postgres_data:
  redis_data:
```

## 📊 Monitoring & Health Checks

### Health Check Configuration
```yaml
# Health checks for all services
services:
  backend:
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "curl", "-f", "http://localhost:8080/api/health"]
      interval: 30s
      timeout: 10s
      start_period: 30s
      retries: 3

  postgres:
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U videohelper_user -d videohelper"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5

  redis:
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "redis-cli", "ping"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 3
```

### Monitoring Stack (Optional)
Add Prometheus and Grafana for monitoring:

```yaml
# Additional monitoring services
  prometheus:
    image: prom/prometheus
    ports:
      - "9090:9090"
    volumes:
      - ./prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml
      - prometheus_data:/prometheus
    command:
      - '--config.file=/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml'
      - '--storage.tsdb.path=/prometheus'

  grafana:
    image: grafana/grafana
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    volumes:
      - grafana_data:/var/lib/grafana
    environment:
      - GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin
```

## 🔒 Security Configuration

### Production Security
```yaml
# Production security settings
services:
  backend:
    environment:
      - API_KEY=${API_KEY}  # Set strong API key
      - JWT_SECRET_KEY=${JWT_SECRET_KEY}  # Set strong JWT secret
      - RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=60
      - CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com
    # Remove debug volumes in production
    # volumes: []

  postgres:
    environment:
      - POSTGRES_PASSWORD=${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}  # Use strong password
    # Don't expose port in production
    # ports: []

  redis:
    command: redis-server --requirepass ${REDIS_PASSWORD}
    environment:
      - REDIS_PASSWORD=${REDIS_PASSWORD}
```

### SSL/TLS Configuration
```yaml
# Add reverse proxy with SSL
  nginx:
    image: nginx:alpine
    ports:
      - "80:80"
      - "443:443"
    volumes:
      - ./nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf
      - ./ssl:/etc/nginx/ssl
    depends_on:
      - backend
      - frontend
```

## 📈 Scaling Configuration

### Horizontal Scaling
```yaml
# Scale backend services
services:
  backend:
    deploy:
      replicas: 3
      resources:
        limits:
          cpus: '2'
          memory: 4G
        reservations:
          cpus: '1'
          memory: 2G

  # Load balancer
  nginx:
    image: nginx:alpine
    volumes:
      - ./nginx-lb.conf:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf
    depends_on:
      - backend
```

### Resource Limits
```yaml
# Resource management
services:
  backend:
    deploy:
      resources:
        limits:
          cpus: '4'
          memory: 8G
        reservations:
          cpus: '2'  
          memory: 4G
    ulimits:
      nofile:
        soft: 65536
        hard: 65536
```

## 🛠️ Development Workflow

### Development Override
Create `docker/docker-compose.dev.yml`:

```yaml
# Development overrides
version: '3.8'

services:
  backend:
    volumes:
      - ../backend:/app/backend:ro
    environment:
      - DEBUG_MODE=true
      - LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
      - RELOAD=true
    command: ["uvicorn", "backend.app:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8080", "--reload"]

  frontend:
    volumes:
      - ../frontend/src:/app/src:ro
    command: ["npm", "run", "dev", "--", "--host", "0.0.0.0"]
```

### Development Commands
```bash
# Start development environment
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml -f docker/docker-compose.dev.yml up

# View logs
docker compose logs -f backend
docker compose logs -f frontend

# Execute commands in containers
docker compose exec backend python -c "print('Hello')"
docker compose exec postgres psql -U videohelper_user -d videohelper

# Rebuild specific service
docker compose build backend
docker compose up -d backend
```

## 🔧 Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

#### Database Connection Issues
```bash
# Check database connectivity
docker compose exec backend python -c "
from backend.database import get_job_store
store = get_job_store()
print('Database connected successfully')
"

# Check database tables
docker compose exec postgres psql -U videohelper_user -d videohelper -c "\dt"
```

#### Permission Issues
```bash
# Fix volume permissions
sudo chown -R $USER:$USER output/ cache/ logs/

# Or use Docker user mapping
services:
  backend:
    user: "${UID}:${GID}"
```

#### Memory Issues
```bash
# Monitor container resource usage
docker stats

# Increase container limits
services:
  backend:
    deploy:
      resources:
        limits:
          memory: 8G
```

### Debugging Commands
```bash
# View container logs
docker compose logs -f --tail=100 backend

# Execute shell in container
docker compose exec backend bash

# Check service health
docker compose ps
docker compose exec backend curl http://localhost:8080/api/health

# Monitor resource usage
docker compose exec backend htop
```

## 🚀 Production Deployment

### Production Checklist
- [ ] Set strong passwords for all services
- [ ] Configure SSL/TLS certificates
- [ ] Set up proper backup strategy
- [ ] Configure log rotation
- [ ] Set up monitoring and alerting
- [ ] Test disaster recovery procedures
- [ ] Configure firewall rules
- [ ] Set up regular security updates

### Backup Strategy
```bash
# Database backup
docker compose exec postgres pg_dump -U videohelper_user videohelper > backup.sql

# Volume backup
docker run --rm -v ai-video-generator_postgres_data:/data -v $(pwd):/backup alpine tar czf /backup/postgres_backup.tar.gz /data
```

### Update Strategy
```bash
# Rolling update
docker compose pull
docker compose up -d --no-deps backend
docker compose up -d --no-deps frontend
```

Always test deployments in a staging environment before production deployment.